Descrizione The Domus Foundation, a Valaisan institution for psychosocial rehabilitation, accompanies adults facing major mental disorders. Nearly 150 employees are committed to it with conviction and professionalism. Our vision: self-determination for everyone, a solution-centric approach and professional practices marked by benevolence and responsibility. We seek for our home in Ardon a.e.: Nurse in Psychiatry (60%) from July 1 or to agree ## Mansioni
• ensure daily nursing care of the persons accompanied in their entirety, at the preventive, curative, medico-educational and palliative level, if necessary;
• managing all medical consultations and continuity of care;
• providing support to beneficiaries within the Foyer d'Ardon in their daily activities with a view to psychosocial rehabilitation based on self-determination;
• support residents in their individual projects and objectives;
• develop a privileged relationship with the network of accompanying persons;
• collaborate in interprofessionality with social workers, ESAs, ASSCs, day centres and workshops. ## Cosa offeriamo
• join a foundation guided by participatory management, positive dynamics and a strong spirit of openness;
• to integrate an institution certified by Promotion Santé Suisse, concerned with the well-being of everyone and the teams where listening, collaboration, mutual assistance and friendliness are cultivated;
• to take your place in a structure that regularly carries out many projects to which everyone can contribute;
• to benefit from annual scheduled working hours and collaboration within a multidisciplinary team;
• to benefit from a pleasant working environment and good social and wage conditions;
• Continuing training every year via our training catalogue "Acting Together". ## Requisiti
• you benefit from a Bachelor of Nursing or equivalent, CAS psychiatrist an asset;
• you have at least 2 years' professional experience. Knowledge of the RAI (Resident Assessment Instrument) software is an asset;
• with a sense of organisation, management of priorities, you like to work as a team but also independently, you appreciate versatility;
• you master the usual computer tools (MS Office);
• holder of a driving licence, you have a private vehicle. # Interested Contatto? Additional information can be obtained at 027 205 75 00. Please send us your complete file with CV, photo, cover letter, diplomas and work certificates by May 15, 2026. The files will be treated confidentially.

